# Target A §177.5B gate floor is vacuous under the canonical populations

**Date:** 2026-10-04<br>
**Classification:** exact regression candidate; unreviewed lifecycle.<br>
**Target A / Level I status:** open.

## Provenance and scope

This note extracts the unique gate-floor regression from closed PR [#577](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/e-99/pull/577), source branch `swarm/codex-a-sector-source-20260925` at `b41edc61033d9b597252eb499a43920a3cd78267`. Its unit-contact midpoint-confinement result is omitted here because the related one-source-arm-per-contact-edge theorem was preserved in main through #648. The statement below concerns only the displayed lower bound in Target A Section 177.5B. It does not assert that canonical configurations have no actual gates.

## Packing bounds

Let `K` be a planar convex body of diameter `d` and perimeter `P`. For any unit-separated finite set `X` contained in `K` with `dist(x,partial K)<1` for every `x in X`,

\[
|X|\le {8P\over\pi}+1\le 8d+1.
\tag{1}
\]

For any unit-separated finite set `O` outside `K` with `dist(o,K)<1` for every `o in O`,

\[
|O|\le {8P\over\pi}+9\le 8d+9.
\tag{2}
\]

To see (1), place disjoint open radius-`1/2` disks around the points of `X`. Their union lies in `(K+\tfrac12 B)\setminus(K\ominus\tfrac32 B)`. The outer Steiner shell has area `P/2+pi/4`; the inner layer removed has area at most `3P/2`, by coarea and monotonicity of inner parallel perimeters. Hence the union area is at most `2P+pi/4`. Each disk has area `pi/4`, giving `|X|<=8P/pi+1`.

For (2), the disks lie in `(K+\tfrac32 B)\setminus(K\ominus\tfrac12 B)`. The outer shell has area `3P/2+9pi/4`, and the inner layer has area at most `P/2`, so the union area is at most `2P+9pi/4`. Division by `pi/4` gives `|O|<=8P/pi+9`. The final inequalities in both cases use Cauchy's convex-perimeter bound `P<=pi d`. The inner-layer estimates also hold when the inner parallel body disappears before the indicated offset: integrate the nonincreasing inner perimeter only up to its extinction depth.

## Consequence for the displayed canonical gate floor

In the canonical Section 177 setup, `C^partial` is a subset of the unit-separated response set and each of its points is less than one from `partial K^*`; every point of `O` is outside `K^*` at distance less than one. Applying (1) and (2) separately gives

\[
|C^partial|+|O|\le16d+10<20d+25.
\]

Therefore the Section 177.5B formula

\[
G_{CO}\ge {1\over10}\max\{0,|C^partial|+|O|-20d-25\}
\]

reduces to `G_CO >= 0` for every canonical configuration. It cannot guarantee a positive number of source gates at its stated constants. This does not prove `G_CO=0`, and it does not remove actual gates from a particular source. The route still needs a sharper overlap bound or a source-to-Schur / strict-competitor theorem.

No theorem-state, Target A route, or prompt is changed by this report. Independent audit is needed before altering how Section 177.5B is used in the active route.
